  "body": "## Issue\nCloses #1380\nClaim: cloud/i1380-fable\nAuthor model: Fable 5.2 (cloud/i1380-fable)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/i1380-opus-review)\n\n## What and why\nThe previous hero (the forum page pulled into an iPhone with a genie effect) was judged too conventional. Three concepts were posted on #1380; the operator chose **A « the lens » for the README hero** and **B « `:o` » for the GitHub social preview**, with one condition: the phone must show the real app.\n\n- `docs/assets/hero.jpg` (2400×1200, about 410 KB): the forum's home page as a printed sheet on an orange table, a phone lying on it showing the same categories in the app. Built from `docs/assets/source/hero.html`.\n- `docs/assets/social-preview.png` (1280×640, about 70 KB): the forum's smiley code as a two-ink typographic poster with the wordmark. Built from `docs/assets/source/social.html`.\n- `node render.js` writes both in place, lowers the JPEG quality until the hero is at most 500 KB, and fails on a missing font or an image that did not load.\n- **The phone screen is an image slot.** `render.js` uses the simulator capture `docs/assets/source/app-forums.png` when it exists. **It does not exist yet: the committed `hero.jpg` is built with a stand-in** (`app-screen.html`, drawn from the app's list code, sources listed at the top of the file; not a screenshot). When the Mac session pushes the capture, `node render.js` is run again and `hero.jpg` replaced, on this PR or a follow-up.\n- `hfr.webp` keeps only the category, sub-category and counter columns.\n- README alt text and `docs/assets/source/README.md` (recipe, licences, the source of « 1997 ») updated; the old `scene.html` and the concept folder are removed.\n\n**For the operator after the merge:** upload `docs/assets/social-preview.png` in the repository's Settings › Social preview (a repository setting, not done by this PR).\n\nWhy no wider: docs and images only; no `App/` or `Packages/` file.\n\n## How it was verified\n- `node docs/assets/source/render.js` reproduces both committed images (the reviewer ran it in a copy: byte for byte).\n- Sizes: `hero.jpg` 2400×1200 under 500 KB; `social-preview.png` 1280×640 under 1 MB.\n- Failure modes run in a copy: without `App/` (stand-in icons missing) and without `hfr.webp`: exit 1, nothing written.\n- Both images looked at after each render; fonts are Inter and JetBrains Mono (SIL OFL 1.1), downloaded by the recipe and not committed.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (docs only)\n- [ ] Tests added/updated: not applicable (images and their sources); `render.js` checks its own inputs and the size limit\n- [x] No secrets; no member name, avatar or post in either image\n- [x] Docs updated (`docs/assets/source/README.md`, README alt text); after the merge #1380 is closed by hand with `Done in #PR (merged as <sha>)`\n- [x] Author model: Fable 5.2 / Reviewer model: Opus 5.5\n- [x] No legacy behaviour or gap row: no `### Ledger` section\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFCzRPyvvWgrdKeDb8",
