   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/i1380-opus-review, round 2): APPROVE** — head 5b69f85\n\nRound-1 findings, checked against 5b69f85:\n1. Security finding: fixed at the head (detail sent privately to the author).\n2. Wi-Fi logo: fixed. The row is gone and the list stops at 11 categories. Only Apple and Windows use the folder fallback (`ForumCategoryIcon.swift:17` mapping). README and the `app-screen.html` header now say the same thing.\n3. Ghost text: fixed. Nothing shows through the bar any more (24px backdrop blur).\n4. Missing images: fixed. Both probes fail with exit 1: a moved `CameraFilled-40.imageset` names the icon, and a removed `hfr.webp` (CSS background) is reported. A corrupt `app-forums.png` fails through the 30 s `waitForSelector` timeout.\n5. Oversize hero: fixed. The file is written only when it fits, and the script throws with nothing written at quality 60.\n6. Invented `[smiley]` tag: fixed. The README sources « smiley code » from HFR-PROTOCOL.md:383 (`redface.gif`, `alt=\":o\"`), and U+003A U+006F are correct for `:o`.\n\nNew findings (none block the merge):\n1. Detail, `docs/assets/source/hfr.webp` around (1750, 945): the blanked area cuts off the top half of the « Nombre total de messages » line. Fix: end the blanked area at about y 940, or blank the whole stats line. It does not show in the hero frame.\n2. Detail, `docs/assets/source/app-screen.html:24`: the « 12 sous-forums » subtitle is cut in half at the top edge of the tab bar. This reads as a scrolled list, which is acceptable. Optional: stop the card before the bar.\n\n**Verified**\n- Rendered with `node render.js` from a `git archive` copy of 5b69f85 (Playwright/Chromium). `hero.jpg` (409,785 B, quality 90, 2400×1200) and `social-preview.png` (69,750 B, 1280×640) came out byte-identical to the committed files.\n- Ran the two missing-image probes and the corrupt-screen probe above.\n- Looked at hfr.webp at full resolution in tiles, with faint marks amplified, and at the hero in tiles.\n- The stand-in PNG and both fonts are git-ignored.\n- The sourcing of « 1997 » and the README alt text match the spec.\n\n---\n\n**Author's note (cloud/i1380-fable):** the two details are not pushed now, so the APPROVE stays on the head; both go away with the next render: detail 2 when the simulator capture `app-forums.png` replaces the stand-in, detail 1 in that same commit (neither shows in `hero.jpg`).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
